  "history_summaries": [
    "Round 1: Fixed assertion `grant_valid_when_serving` (assertion_error). Root cause: timing mismatch — `grant` is registered (RegInit), so its value assigned in sAssegna only appears after the clock edge, but the assertion checked `grant.orR` in the same cycle, seeing the stale (zero) value. Fix: introduced `check_grant = RegNext(in_assegna && any_fu && coda0_valid, false.B)` to defer the condition check by one cycle, then assert `!check_grant || grant.orR`. The grant value assigned in sAssegna is now checked one cycle later when it is stable at the register output. Assertion label `grant_valid_when_serving` preserved. No homologous assertions found: the other two assertions (`request_eventually_granted`, `pending_request_eventually_served`) use `astRelaxedLiveness` which is structurally different (bounded-liveness check, not same-cycle fvAssert).",
    "Round 2: Fixed DUT bug — fu bits never cleared upon grant issuance in sAssegna state (lines 95-104 of b03.scala). Root cause: when the state machine served a request from the queue head and issued a grant, the corresponding fu (follow-up) bit remained asserted. This had two cascading effects: (1) prevented re-queuing of persistently active requests in the next sAnalisReq cycle because `ruN && !fuN` evaluated false, and (2) created windows where `any_fu=1` and `any_grant=0` (empty queue after shift, stale fu) triggering spurious liveness timer capture for `pending_request_eventually_served`. Fix: added `fu1 := false.B`, `fu2 := false.B`, `fu3 := false.B`, `fu4 := false.B` inside the respective `is(U1)` through `is(U4)` cases of the `switch(coda0)` in sAssegna. This ensures that once a request is served its pending flag is immediately cleared, allowing proper re-enqueuing of sustained inputs and eliminating spurious liveness windows. The fix also addresses the shared root cause of `request_eventually_granted` failures (same stale-fu pipeline stall). Assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
    "Round 3: Fixed DUT bug in sAnalisReq — unconditional fu assignments (fu1:=ru1..fu4:=ru4) at lines 85-88 caused fu bits to be set for ALL requests even when only the highest-priority one was enqueued by the priority encoder. This created a livelock: e.g., fu4 was set when U3 was enqueued; fu4 had no queue entry and could never be served. Fix: moved each fu assignment inside the corresponding priority-encoder conditional branch (fu1:=true.B inside ru1&&!fu1 when-branch, etc.), and removed the unconditional fu1:=ru1..fu4:=ru4 block. This ensures only the actually-enqueued request gets its fu bit set, preventing stuck-fu scenarios. Also addresses the shared root cause of `request_eventually_granted` failures (stale fu → no enqueue → no grant). Assertion labels preserved unchanged."
  ],
